From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haseenesss <haseenesss@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:55:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] 13 Sentinels (Asia): the main thread waits for the render
 thread instead of skipping the frame

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#2936
Reason: the game crashes at its first frame when the start is slow (a library folder on a USB 2.0 disk)

At the end of a frame the main thread waits for the render thread only as
long as the frame's time lasts (main+0x30c194), then goes on without it. The
render thread's first submission waits on the host for the pipeline archive
and the prepare step. From a library folder on a USB 2.0 disk that wait was
7 s and more, the main thread ran on meanwhile, and the render thread's first
draws bound a texture entry of index -1: SIGSEGV at main+0x309128, in 13 of
13 starts with a wait of 7 s or more and in none of 8 below 6.5 s (Mac, M2,
8 GB).

patches.py cuts the three branches that end the wait in the 1.00 build of
main, so the main thread waits until the render thread is done. 9 of 9 starts
ran with the cut. The rewriter's output with it is the binary that was tested.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1411

